# The relay's image builds from the REPOSITORY ROOT, because its crate depends on `konclave-http`
# and a Docker build cannot reach outside its context (see relay-server/Dockerfile). Without this
# file that context is the whole tree, including an 18 GB `target/`.
#
# Deny everything, then re-admit only what the build reads. Written this way round on purpose: a new
# directory appearing at the root is excluded by default, so the context cannot quietly grow. The
# cost is that a genuinely new dependency must be added here as well as to the Dockerfile, and that
# cost is the point - it fails at build time rather than shipping something nobody meant to send.
*

!konclave-http
!relay-server

# Build output inside the admitted crates. `target/` is gitignored, so `railway up` never uploads it,
# but a local `docker build` has no such filter and would otherwise copy gigabytes per attempt.
konclave-http/target
relay-server/target
